// THE STRICT RULING (Eric, 2026-08-13, completing the day's clean-
// dataflow arc): if any element computation generates bottom, the
// collection result is bottom — everywhere, both engines. A produced
// value is never internally mixed-freshness; `map` agrees with the
// hand-written array literal (constructors propagate bottom); the
// downstream last-good holding users actually want is the STORE's
// job (a bottom never overwrites a standing value, so consumers
// pause rather than blank). Per-element failure that is EXPECTED
// should be a value (`/?`, `$`, error variants) — the language's
// standing error philosophy.
//
// Retired with it: the kernel's in_ride_scope op-site taint caches
// (loop bodies + guard interiors — the 2026-07-04 interior-bottom
// cache contract's last remnants) and the interp MapQ slot
// bottom-ride. The designated rides are now exactly: select
// scrutinee, guard FINAL value, `~`'s held arg, tail-rebind formals.
//
// This witness: the fold callback's `v0 / in0` div0s at in0=0; the
// kernel's loop-scoped op cache rode the previous quotient and
// completed the fold with a value ([1:6]) where the interp's op
// poisoned per dense — first exposed by the aug13f first-hour
// generate lanes (the aug05i lesson, again).
// schedule-v1: cap=160 events=1280; in0=i64:-1; in0=i64:0; in0=i64:1; in0=i64:12; in0=i64:5; in0=i64:3
{let v0: i64 = array::fold([i64:7], (i64:-1 / in0), |v0, in0| (v0 / in0)); let v1: Array<i64> = []; v1 <- in0 ~ array::push(v1, in0); let v2 = array::len(v1); ((v2 - v0) + v2)}
